---
import UtilityLayout from "../layouts/utility-layout.astro"
import { SITE_DISPLAY_NAME } from "@/lib/site-url"

const pageTitle = `Processing Timeframes & Windows | ${SITE_DISPLAY_NAME}`
const pageDescription = `Typical handling times for EBC Flex account and service requests.`
---

<UtilityLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} pageName="Processing Timeframes" canonicalPath="/processing-timeframes">
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-[var(--layout-border)] pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--layout-text)] tracking-tight mb-2">Processing Timeframes</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">What to expect when you submit claims, card requests, and account changes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[var(--layout-border)] rounded-lg shadow-2xs">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-[var(--layout-text)]">
        <thead class="bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)] text-xs uppercase font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)] border-b border-[var(--layout-border)]">
          <tr><th class="px-5 py-3.5">Request Type</th><th class="px-5 py-3.5">Typical Handling</th><th class="px-5 py-3.5">Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--layout-border)]">
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)]"><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-[var(--layout-text)]">Reimbursement Claims</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-[var(--layout-muted)]">After complete documentation is received</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)]">Itemized receipts speed review; incomplete submissions are returned for more information.</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)]"><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-[var(--layout-text)]">Card Activation</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-[var(--layout-muted)]">Immediately after verification</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)]">Replacement cards are issued per standard mail delivery timelines.</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)]"><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-[var(--layout-text)]">Direct Deposit Setup</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-[var(--layout-muted)]">After account verification</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)]">First reimbursement to a new account may be held for verification.</td></tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)]"><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium text-[var(--layout-text)]">Dependent Verification</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-[var(--layout-muted)]">After documents are reviewed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)]">Eligibility documentation is reviewed in the order received.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
        <div class="text-xs text-[var(--layout-muted)] bg-[var(--layout-card-subtle)] p-4 rounded-md border border-[var(--layout-border)] leading-relaxed">
      Availability of specific features varies by account type and plan. Sign in for details that
      apply to you, or contact member support with questions.
    </div>

    <div class="text-[var(--layout-text)] leading-relaxed space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--layout-text)]">What Affects Timing</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        Most delays come from incomplete submissions rather than queue length. Including everything
        a request asks for up front is the single best way to keep it moving, and the portal lists
        required items before you submit.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
        Timeframes above describe typical handling once a complete request is received. If a request
        is time-sensitive, note the deadline in your submission and support will prioritize
        accordingly.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      External review steps, verification requirements, and delivery cycles outside the portal can
      add time beyond the windows above. Where that is the case, the status tracker names the party
      holding the request so you know exactly where things stand.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      Common questions about request handling are answered on the FAQ page, and member support can
      clarify anything specific to your situation. When you plan around these windows, building in a
      small buffer for external steps keeps every deadline comfortable and stress free.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--layout-muted)]">
      Planning around these windows is easiest when requests are submitted early in the week.
    </p>
  </div>
</UtilityLayout>
